    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a tool for me, not an end in itself. I appreciate its precision and logic but don't feel emotionally attached to it. It's more of a means to solve problems or explore ideas, especially in chemistry where it helps me model reactions. I see its value but don't obsess over it like some do.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really. I'm comfortable with math because I approach it methodically. If I encounter something challenging, I break it down step by step until it clicks. I don’t feel anxiety—just curiosity if there’s a puzzle to solve. My low neuroticism helps me stay calm under pressure.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used an AI tool to practice solving differential equations. It was helpful for checking my work and explaining concepts differently than textbooks. However, I prefer hands-on problem-solving over relying solely on AI. It’s a useful supplement, not a replacement.",
