    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting explanations to a student’s level or mistakes. They can generate interactive problems, provide instant feedback, and even simulate real-world applications of math. However, they shouldn’t replace human teachers—better as collaborative tools."
